    "created_at": "2021-04-30T17:13:20Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-04-30T17:13:20Z",
    "body": "@ricea is the request to relax spec behavior to make erroring the stream achievable, or allow it to outlive the source realm?\r\n\r\nThe latter seems undesirable for several reasons:\r\n 1. Surprising semantic difference between native stream vs non-native, non-optimized native, and pipes with a combination.\r\n 2. Confusion around lifespan of source.\r\n 2. Privacy issues with sources from powerful APIs (a camera/mic track outliving its page and privacy indicators).",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
